# No single-use helpers

Do not add a function, method, or local `def` that has one call site. Write that code at the call site.

A helper is worth it when at least two call sites use it, or when a name is the only way to say something the surrounding code cannot. One call site does not qualify. Wrapping one line (a unit conversion, a `getState`, a tensor build) makes the diff longer and the review harder to follow.

```python
# Bad — defined once, called once
def _positions_nm(quantity):
    return np.asarray(quantity.value_in_unit(unit.nanometer), dtype=np.float64)

positions = _positions_nm(inpcrd.positions)

# Good
positions = np.asarray(
    inpcrd.positions.value_in_unit(unit.nanometer), dtype=np.float64
)
```
